  "research_notes": "Current core dataset-specific accepted associations: WRN/MSI-high accepted and independently validated globally, robust across high/low TMB, high Cas9, high screen quality, KY, matched RNA/DNA, growth/lineage strata. SMARCA2/SMARCA4-loss accepted and independently validated in ARID1A-intact and ARID1A-loss settings, robust across high Cas9, high TMB, high screen quality, KY, matched RNA/DNA, growth/lineage strata. NFE2L2/KEAP1-loss accepted globally via reversal, validated in STK11-intact, robust across STK11-loss, high Cas9, fast growth, high screen quality, KY, matched RNA/DNA. Newly accepted pending validation: STAT3 stronger dependency in PTEN-loss lines, H93/R61 signed effect +0.267, interval +0.215 to +0.319, far above approximate STAT3 clinical threshold 0.028; validation requested because this is a new large association and multiplicity/confounding remain possible. Negative or unsupported: BRAF V600E stronger BRAF, EGFR amp stronger EGFR after validation, KRAS mutation stronger RIT1, MYC amp stronger RPL11, PIK3CA mutation stronger STAT3, NF1 KRAS-WT stronger RIT1, BRAF KRAS-WT stronger RIT1, ERBB2 amp stronger ERBB2 among EGFR-negative KRAS-WT lines, STK11 loss stronger KRAS. Unresolved but closed: EGFR amp stronger EGFR among ERBB2-negative KRAS-WT lines; MYC amp stronger TMED10 among high MYC expression; RB1 loss stronger KIF18A; interactions SMARCA4 x ARID1A and KEAP1 x STK11; USP7 among high MYC expression. Active priorities: PTEN-loss STAT3 robustness and context tests under high Cas9, high screen quality, KY, high/low TMB, PIK3CA-negative, adenocarcinoma. Also maintain broad exploration controls and EGFR reversal only if new interval evidence justifies. Interpret all results as supplied-dataset associations, not causal dependencies or generalizable biology.",
  "narrative": "The new results mainly confirm that the three very large core associations are not sensitive to technical Cas9-activity restriction or biologically motivated subsetting. Approximate 10% clinical thresholds from population absolute mean scores are about +0.030 for WRN, +0.042 for SMARCA2, +0.009 for NFE2L2, +0.028 for STAT3, +0.026 for ERBB2, +0.024 for KRAS, +0.025 for TMED10, and +0.026 for KIF18A. H86/R54 gives WRN/MSI-high a signed effect +0.776 with lower bound +0.728 under high Cas9 activity; H87/R55 gives SMARCA2/SMARCA4-loss +0.788 with lower bound +0.756; H88/R56 gives KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 +0.800 with lower bound +0.769. These are all far above their thresholds and far from null, supporting acceptance and closure. H89/R57 tests WRN/MSI-high among lower mutation-burden lines; despite only 21 exposed lines, the estimate is +0.798 and the lower bound is +0.706. This is valid and strongly supports that MSI-high is not merely acting as a generic high-TMB surrogate in this dataset. H96/R64 and H97/R65 similarly accept SMARCA2/SMARCA4-loss under high mutation burden and KEAP1-loss under faster proliferation. The RTK and transcriptional-MYC isolation tests do not support the registered positive directions as clinically meaningful. H90/R58 has a positive point estimate +0.018 but interval -0.012 to +0.048; because the upper bound crosses the EGFR threshold, it remains unresolved. H91/R59 has upper bound +0.023, below the ERBB2 threshold of about +0.026, so clinically meaningful stronger ERBB2 dependency in the isolated EGFR-negative KRAS-WT context is rejected. H92/R60 is near-null for MYC-related TMED10, interval -0.030 to +0.031, unresolved. H94/R62 has upper bound +0.036 above the KIF18A threshold, but includes null, so RB1-loss stronger KIF18A remains unresolved. H95/R63 has upper bound +0.018 below the KRAS threshold, so STK11-loss stronger KRAS is rejected. The major new finding is H93/R61: PTEN loss is associated with much stronger STAT3 dependency, signed estimate +0.267, interval +0.215 to +0.319, with cells 266 versus 1734. This effect is roughly 9 to 11 times the approximate STAT3 clinical threshold and very precisely estimated, so I accept it in this dataset but keep it active because it is a newly discovered association with multiplicity and confounding concerns. I request independent validation of H93 rather than H7 because H7's global SMARCA2 effect is already supported by multiple accepted and validated context refinements, whereas H93 is a new large claim whose internal validity would be most directly strengthened by independent replication. These remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
}

