  "research_notes": "Updated dataset-specific accepted associations: WRN/MSI-high is dramatically stronger WRN dependency, globally validated and robust across multiple strata. SMARCA4-loss is dramatically stronger SMARCA2 dependency, globally accepted, validated in ARID1A-intact and ARID1A-loss contexts, and robust across multiple strata. KEAP1-loss is dramatically weaker NFE2L2 dependency, globally accepted and robust. PTEN-loss is substantially stronger STAT3 dependency, globally accepted and independently validated; newly accepted in PIK3CA- and TP53-intact context H112/R70, with independent validation requested for H112. Rejected registered positive directions in this batch: H110 TP53-loss PTEN/STAT3 amplification, H114 KY-library WRN/MSI-high amplification, H117 adenocarcinoma SMARCA2/SMARCA4-loss amplification, H120 PTEN-loss stronger KRAS. Registered opposite attenuation follow-ups: PTEN/STAT3 attenuation in TP53-loss and WRN/MSI-high attenuation in KY library. Unresolved interaction follow-ups: H109 PIK3CA PTEN/STAT3 interaction, H111 KRAS PTEN/STAT3 interaction, H113 MDM2 TP53/CDKN2A interaction, H115 WRN adenocarcinoma interaction, H116 SMARCA2 KY interaction, H118 NFE2L2 KY interaction, H119 NFE2L2 adenocarcinoma interaction. Multiplicity remains high and interaction tests are often underpowered; accept only large precise effects or validation. Interpret all findings as associations in the supplied lung cell-line dataset, not causal dependencies or generalizable biology.",
