  "narrative": "The current evidence base supports five dataset-specific marker-dependency associations: MSI-high with far stronger WRN dependency, SMARCA4 loss with far stronger SMARCA2 dependency, KEAP1 loss with far weaker NFE2L2 dependency, PTEN loss with substantially stronger STAT3 dependency, and CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency. The next scientifically useful step is not to re-open accepted large-effect axes unless needed for marker independence, but to characterize the newly accepted CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 axis and to test two remaining driver-gene borderline signals. For CDKN2A-loss/MDM2, I register robustness and specificity refinements. Screen-batch interaction asks whether the effect is batch-specific; the KY-library mean difference asks whether it persists outside the dominant Avana library; slow-growth, high-MYC-expression, and KRAS-intact contexts ask whether the association is modified by proliferation state, transcriptional MYC program, or KRAS co-alteration. Because global CDKN2A-loss may correlate with other accepted marker losses, I also register specificity probes: in MSI-intact lines, PTEN-intact lines, SMARCA4-intact lines, and a TP53/MSI/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact context, test CDKN2A loss on WRN, STAT3, SMARCA2, and USP7 respectively. Positive signed estimates for direction -1 would mean stronger dependency in CDKN2A-loss lines. If upper bounds fall below the approximate 10-percent thresholds, these probes reject clinically meaningful cross-marker effects and support CDKN2A/MDM2 specificity; if lower bounds exceed the thresholds, CDKN2A loss should be interpreted as part of a broader dependency phenotype rather than an MDM2-specific marker. For the TP53-loss uncertainty around CDKN2A/MDM2, I register a cleaner TP53-loss context excluding MSI, KEAP1, and PTEN alterations. This should help determine whether the TP53-loss-specific effect remains above the MDM2 threshold or only weakly excludes null. Finally, I register context refinements for unresolved driver-gene hypotheses: EGFR amplification in ERBB2-intact, TP53-intact lines, motivated by the borderline ERBB2-intact EGFR signal; and KRAS mutation in adenocarcinoma, TP53-intact lines, motivated by the absence of a global KRAS-mutation effect. For dependency outcomes, a more negative score is stronger dependency. Direction -1 hypotheses encode stronger dependency in the exposed group as raw negative contrasts, displayed as positive signed evidence. Interpretation remains association-only in the supplied lung cell-line dataset and does not imply causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted/validated dataset-specific axes: MSI-high -> far stronger WRN dependency (R6/R53); SMARCA4 loss -> far stronger SMARCA2 dependency (R7 plus many contexts); KEAP1 loss -> far weaker NFE2L2 dependency (direction +1 R8/R26/R45/R46/R56); PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency (R61/R66, R70/R79, R84); CDKN2A loss -> stronger MDM2 dependency (R92/R93, R94, R102). H161 is accepted but active because discovery and validation are direction-consistent, while validation lower bound is near zero and below threshold in TP53-loss lines. Approximate 10-percent thresholds: MDM2 +0.027, STAT3 +0.028, WRN +0.030, SMARCA2 +0.042, USP7 +0.018, EGFR +0.025, KRAS +0.0245. New registered claims focus on CDKN2A/MDM2 robustness and specificity: batch interaction, KY-library context, slow-growth context, high MYC expression, KRAS-intact context, and a clean TP53-loss context excluding MSI/KEAP1/PTEN. Specificity probes test CDKN2A loss on WRN in MSI-intact lines, STAT3 in PTEN-intact lines, SMARCA2 in SMARCA4-intact lines, and USP7 in TP53/MSI/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact lines. For specificity probes, rejection when upper bound is below threshold supports outcome specificity; acceptance when lower bound is above threshold argues against specificity and toward a broader CDKN2A dependency phenotype; intervals spanning threshold remain unresolved. Driver refinements register EGFR amplification in ERBB2-intact, TP53-intact lines and KRAS mutation in adenocarcinoma, TP53-intact lines. Analyze should prioritize the TP53-loss clean CDKN2A/MDM2 context and specificity probes, then batch/library/growth/MYC/KRAS-context robustness tests, then EGFR and KRAS refinements if slots remain. Independent validation requests remain limited; reserve them only if a refined CDKN2A/MDM2 or EGFR/KRAS refinement becomes direction-consistent and near or above threshold after discovery assessment. Do not infer causality or generalizability."
}

