  "narrative": "Due assessments and validation response: H187 (TP53 loss vs TP53 intact on dependency_USP7, direction +1) is accepted and closed. Discovery R123 estimated +0.396 (95% Welch +0.325 to +0.467); independent validation R132 estimated +0.394 with stringent independent interval +0.289 to +0.499. Because the reported estimates are signed to direction +1, TP53-loss lines have higher, i.e. less negative, USP7 dependency scores, indicating weaker USP7 dependency. The intervals are far above the approximate 10-percent absolute-mean USP7 threshold near +0.018, so this is a strong supplied-dataset association. H161 (CDKN2A loss vs intact within TP53-loss on dependency_MDM2, direction -1) remains accepted but active. Discovery R95 estimated +0.111 (95% Welch +0.035 to +0.186), above the approximate MDM2 clinical threshold near +0.027. Independent validation R106 estimated +0.115 with stringent interval +0.002 to +0.227, confirming direction and not excluding clinically meaningful large effects, but its lower bound is near zero and below the 10-percent threshold, so the clinically meaningful magnitude specifically in TP53-loss lines is not precisely established. This does not undermine the global validated CDKN2A-loss/MDM2 association H146. Final report: supported dataset-specific associations are MSI-high/stronger WRN (R6, R53), SMARCA4-loss/stronger SMARCA2 (R7, R14, R39, R40, R49), KEAP1-loss/weaker NFE2L2 (R8, R18, R26, R83), PTEN-loss/stronger STAT3 including clean contexts (R61, R66, R70, R79, R84), CDKN2A-loss/stronger MDM2 globally (R92, R93) and robust contexts (R102, R110-R113, R108), and newly TP53-loss/weaker USP7 (R123, R132). Negative or unsupported include BRAF V600E on BRAF, EGFR amplification globally on EGFR, ERBB2 amplification on ERBB2, KRAS mutation/NF1 loss/STK11 loss/PTEN loss on KRAS, broad MYC amplification effects, MYC amplification with high expression on RPL11, and CDKN2A cross-marker effects on WRN/STAT3/SMARCA2 in targeted contexts. Unresolved: TP53-loss-specific CDKN2A-MDM2 magnitude (H161, H183), USP7 specificity relative to CDKN2A/TP53 co-alteration and assay quality (H185, H196, H200), high-quality CDKN2A-by-TP53 interaction on MDM2 (H186, H184), borderline EGFR signals in ERBB2/TP53-intact contexts, and some lineage/library/growth modifiers with wide intervals. Most informative next analyses are not additional broad driver screening but precision/context tests already active: H184 for CDKN2A-MDM2 in higher-quality TP53-loss screens, H185/H196/H200 for TP53 and CDKN2A specificity/interaction on USP7, and H186 for a higher-quality CDKN2A-by-TP53 interaction on MDM2. All claims are associations in the supplied lung CRISPR dataset, not causal or external-generalizable mechanisms.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 synthesis final. Accepted dataset axes: MSI-high -> stronger WRN; SMARCA4-loss -> stronger SMARCA2; KEAP1-loss -> weaker NFE2L2; PTEN-loss -> stronger STAT3; CDKN2A-loss -> stronger MDM2 globally and robustly; TP53-loss -> weaker USP7 now validated by R132 far above threshold. H161 accepted but active: TP53-loss CDKN2A-MDM2 direction validated but clinical magnitude imprecise (R106 lower near 0). H183 unresolved clean-context precision. USP7 specificity unresolved in co-alteration/screen-quality contexts (H185, H196, H200). High-quality interaction H186 and H184 are the most informative next analyses. Validation budget exhausted; future work should use discovery precision/context analyses, not broad driver screening. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations, not causality or generalizability."
